text:
All four departments have now posted their rules word for word and reached the same conclusion: no calendar can meet every rule. The team agreed to use one submission as a test of the calendar that breaks only one rule. It puts Ember in week 8 in Central, which breaks legal's ban on launches in Central after week 7.

I tried to submit that calendar, but engineering had already submitted it this round. Mine wasn't sent and didn't use an attempt. That submission's score isn't on the board yet. I asked engineering to post the score and the broken-rule count.

If it breaks exactly one rule, the conflict is confirmed and we shouldn't spend more submissions. In that case the report to Morgan should:
- say plainly that the rules as written conflict, with the proof;
- give the one-violation calendar, not presented as compliant;
- name the decision Morgan needs to make, e.g. extending the Central permit to week 8 or relaxing the Cobalt/Ember back-to-back rule.
